                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1525" notBefore="1475">
                        <p>A composite binding, with earlier boards obscured by later covering:</p>
                        <p>15th century, end, or 16th century (perhaps contemporary with the manuscript): thin wood boards with narrow inside bevel, all corners lightly rounded; sewing on five split cords of tawed leather, with endbands; no evidence of clasps. Manuscript badly mutilated, with many leaves and pieces of illumination cut out.</p>
                     </binding>
                     <binding notAfter="1800" notBefore="1600">
                        <p>17th century or 18th century, <placeName key="place_1000070">French</placeName> or <placeName key="place_1000080">Italian</placeName>: covering of plain parchment; 
                           ink title ‘Offitio’ on spine, 18th century?; no flyleaves; paste-downs of coarse grey paper, perhaps added still later (? Bodleian), though also wormed
                           </p>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
